{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784202255,"nonce":"MECv4/BwhJny3kXWCBx/ZLf+JGk=","title":"The `clone` built-in step kind (ADR-0008, ADR-0045) as a first-class citizen of the pipeline IR: authored as `clone: {}`, compiled and validated, with the workspace-root semantics wired into the DAG model. This is the authoring/compile layer only — no execution yet (proven via `scarab-pipeline` unit tests; execution lands in S3/S6).","message":"Per ADR-0045 §Authoring: `clone` is explicit and zero-config — repo/ref/SHA/token are implicit from the run's trigger context. Optional fields: `depth` (default `1`, `full` for complete history), `submodules`, `lfs`, `ref` override. Downstream steps inherit the clone's workspace via `needs` with no new inheritance rule (ADR-0007).\n\nIncludes the lint rule: a `push`/`pull_request` pipeline with no `clone` step emits a non-fatal compile diagnostic (\"steps will run without source\") — the first real rule for `scarab lint`.\n\nToday the IR has only image + `gate` kinds (`crates/scarab-pipeline/src/lib.rs:264-265,1214-1220`).\n\n\n- [ ] `clone: {}` compiles to a distinct IR step kind; `depth`/`submodules`/`lfs`/`ref` parse and validate\n- [ ] A step with `needs: [\u003cclone-id\u003e]` resolves the clone as its workspace root in the compiled IR\n- [ ] `depth` accepts `1` (default) and `full`; invalid values are a compile error\n- [ ] Missing-`clone` on a `push`/`pull_request` pipeline produces a lint warning (non-fatal), surfaced through the compile diagnostics path\n- [ ] Unit tests cover: clone compiles, knobs validate, lint fires and stays non-fatal, repo-less triggers (cron/upstream) do not warn\n\n\nNone - can start immediately","files":null}]}